{
  "section_tags_version": "1",
  "note": "The metatag vocabulary for the lyric artifact. ACE-Step's tutorial calls structure tags 'the most powerful tool in Lyrics' and warns against stacking them, so this file defines both the tags and the grammar that constrains their use. Tags live in the lyrics, not in the caption: the caption is the overall portrait, the lyrics are the temporal script.",
  "grammar": {
    "section_tag": "[<section>] or [<section> - <modifier>]",
    "max_modifiers": 1,
    "max_tags_per_section": 4,
    "max_transitions_per_section": 1,
    "rules": [
      "At most one modifier per section tag. Stacking is explicitly discouraged by the model's own guide: it risks the model singing the tag, and it dilutes the instruction.",
      "A transition belongs to the section it leaves, not the one it enters, and is written as a standalone tag at the end of that section: [drum fill], [riser], [stop]. One per boundary.",
      "Beyond the one hyphenated modifier, up to four standalone performance tags may sit on their own lines directly under a section header -- typically a vocal mode (rap, clean vocal), a register or delivery (belting, raspy), and an energy or emotion (building energy, vulnerable). The guide presents these as their own bracket tags, separate from section headers, which is why they are a different mechanism with a different budget.",
      "A standalone tag applies from where it appears until the next section header.",
      "Separate sections with a blank line, so the boundary is unambiguous.",
      "A written line is not a phrase. Cadence splits lines in the middle, so a caesura marker ( / or | ) may be written inside a line to mark where the sung phrase breaks; it is never sung. Commas, semicolons, colons and dashes are read as weak breaks when no marker is given.",
      "Uppercase within a lyric line means louder, higher-intensity delivery; use it sparingly and never for a whole verse.",
      "Parentheses around a phrase mean background vocal or harmony, not a stage direction.",
      "Keep complex style description in the caption and only the performance instruction in the tag.",
      "A modifier must not contradict the caption: if the caption says 'intimate chamber music', a [Chorus - explosive] tag is a conflict, not a contrast."
    ],
    "not_recognised": "Treat an unrecognised tag as a defect: the model may sing it. The prompt-level check validates every bracket against this file before rendering."
  },
